<title>UK: Bank of Ireland ups step-up FRN to 200 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Bank of Ireland ups step-up FRN to 200 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated floating-rate issue has been increased to 200 million stg from 150 million stg, joint lead managers J.P. Morgan, Lehman Brothers and SBC Warburg said on Friday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Wednesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF IRELAND</p>
<p> AMT    200 MLN STG   SPREAD     *+35 BP   MATURITY   *11.FEB.09</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 BASE	 3M LIBOR  PAY DATE    11.FEB.97</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  A2/A-     ISS PRICE  99.90     FULL FEES   0.40</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK/IE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC   0.20</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>		*FOR FIRST SEVEN YEARS, THEN +85 BP IF NOT CALLED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
